From: Martin Böh <contact@martb.dev>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 03:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH ethtool] ethtool: fix the default EDPD TX interval

The man page says that "--set-phy-tunable DEV energy-detect-power-down
on" without msecs uses the PHY's default TX interval, but the command
always fails with "'msecs' max value is 65533.". The interval starts out
as ETHTOOL_PHY_EDPD_DFLT_TX_MSECS (0xffff), and the range check meant for
a user supplied msecs value rejects it. The default can never be
requested, so the branches marvell10g, adin, bcm54140 and smsc have for
it are unreachable, and a PHY driver that supports only the default
cannot have EDPD enabled at all.

Only range check msecs when it was given. When reading the tunable back,
print the default as such instead of as "TX 65535 msecs".

Fixes: e5684313dbf1 ("ethtool: implement support for Energy Detect Power Down")
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Martin Böh <contact@martb.dev>
---
--- a/ethtool.c
+++ b/ethtool.c
@@ -5457,6 +5457,9 @@ static int do_get_phy_tunable(struct cmd
 		else if (cont.msecs == ETHTOOL_PHY_EDPD_NO_TX)
 			fprintf(stdout,
 				"Energy Detect Power Down: enabled, TX disabled\n");
+		else if (cont.msecs == ETHTOOL_PHY_EDPD_DFLT_TX_MSECS)
+			fprintf(stdout,
+				"Energy Detect Power Down: enabled, default TX interval\n");
 		else
 			fprintf(stdout,
 				"Energy Detect Power Down: enabled, TX %u msecs\n",
@@ -5632,7 +5635,7 @@ static int do_set_phy_tunable(struct cmd
 	u8 ds_changed = 0, ds_has_cnt = 0, ds_enable = 0;
 	u8 fld_changed = 0, fld_enable = 0;
 	u8 fld_msecs = ETHTOOL_PHY_FAST_LINK_DOWN_ON;
-	u8 edpd_changed = 0, edpd_enable = 0;
+	u8 edpd_changed = 0, edpd_enable = 0, edpd_has_msecs = 0;
 	u16 edpd_tx_interval = ETHTOOL_PHY_EDPD_DFLT_TX_MSECS;
 
 	/* Parse arguments */
@@ -5647,7 +5650,8 @@ static int do_set_phy_tunable(struct cmd
 				    &edpd_enable)) {
 		edpd_changed = 1;
 		if (edpd_enable)
-			parse_named_u16(ctx, "msecs", &edpd_tx_interval);
+			edpd_has_msecs = parse_named_u16(ctx, "msecs",
+							 &edpd_tx_interval);
 	} else {
 		exit_bad_args();
 	}
@@ -5675,6 +5679,8 @@ static int do_set_phy_tunable(struct cmd
 	} else if (edpd_changed) {
 		if (!edpd_enable)
 			edpd_tx_interval = ETHTOOL_PHY_EDPD_DISABLE;
+		else if (!edpd_has_msecs)
+			edpd_tx_interval = ETHTOOL_PHY_EDPD_DFLT_TX_MSECS;
 		else if (edpd_tx_interval == 0)
 			edpd_tx_interval = ETHTOOL_PHY_EDPD_NO_TX;
 		else if (edpd_tx_interval > ETHTOOL_PHY_EDPD_NO_TX) {
